    "intro_html":  "This is the rotisserie chicken shortcut done right. You pull the meat off a store bird, fold it into onion, pepper and spinach, and bind the whole thing with a cool tomatillo salsa verde and a blended cottage cheese crema that hits like sour cream for a fraction of the fat. Each burrito lands \u003cstrong\u003eunder 400 calories with a full 4 ounces of meat\u003c/strong\u003e, carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e, and rides on a high fiber tortilla with 18 grams of fiber for about 5 grams of net carb. We already have a Salsa Verde Chicken Burrito Bowl on the site; this is its wrapped cousin, built on pulled rotisserie instead of cooked breast and finished with the cottage cheese crema instead of a plain scoop of rice.",
